{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>To meet Elohim.</b> This teaches that the Shechinah went forth to meet them, like a bridegroom who goes forth to meet the bride — and this is what it says: ״HaShem from Sinai came״ (Deuteronomy 33), and it was not said ״to Sinai He came״ (Mekhilta)." "<b>At the lowest part of the mountain.</b> According to its plain sense: at the foot of the mountain. And its midrash: that the mountain was uprooted from its place and turned over them like a tub (Shabbat 8)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:09.389108219Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}